Sure! To update a break node’s label to `'loopEnd'`, you’ll need to pass the node (in string form) and the new label to the `updateBreak` function. Here’s how you can do it:

```javascript
// Example usage:
const nodeString = /* your break node in string form */;
const result = await functions.updateBreak({
  node: nodeString,
  label: "loopEnd"
});
console.log(result);
```

